#: ../../../src/python/nn/_autosummary/mlx.nn.Upsample.rst:2
msgid "mlx.nn.Upsample"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.12/site-packages/mlx/nn/layers/upsample.py:docstring
#: of mlx.nn.layers.upsample.Upsample:1
msgid "Upsample the input signal spatially."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.12/site-packages/mlx/nn/layers/upsample.py:docstring
#: of mlx.nn.layers.upsample.Upsample:3
msgid ""
"The spatial dimensions are by convention dimensions ``1`` to ``x.ndim - 2``. "
"The first is the batch dimension and the last is the feature dimension."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.12/site-packages/mlx/nn/layers/upsample.py:docstring
#: of mlx.nn.layers.upsample.Upsample:7
msgid ""
"For example, an audio signal would be 3D with 1 spatial dimension, an image "
"4D with 2 and so on and so forth."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.12/site-packages/mlx/nn/layers/upsample.py:docstring
#: of mlx.nn.layers.upsample.Upsample:10
msgid ""
"There are three upsampling algorithms implemented nearest neighbor "
"upsampling, linear interpolation, and cubic interpolation. All can be "
"applied to any number of spatial dimensions. The linear interpolation will "
"be bilinear, trilinear etc when applied to more than one spatial dimension. "
"And cubic interpolation will be bicubic when there are 2 spatial dimensions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.12/site-packages/mlx/nn/layers/upsample.py:docstring
#: of mlx.nn.layers.upsample.Upsample:17
msgid ""
"When using one of the linear or cubic interpolation modes the "
"``align_corners`` argument changes how the corners are treated in the input "
"image. If ``align_corners=True`` then the top and left edge of the input and "
"output will be matching as will the bottom right edge."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.12/site-packages/mlx/nn/layers/upsample.py:docstring
#: of mlx.nn.layers.upsample.Upsample:23
msgid ""
"When ``antialias=True`` is used with ``\"linear\"`` or ``\"cubic\"`` mode, "
"an antialiased filter is applied during downsampling (scale factor < 1), "
"producing smoother results by avoiding aliasing artifacts. For 2D integer-"
"ratio downscales with ``align_corners=False``, this matches the behavior of "
"PyTorch's ``F.interpolate(antialias=True)``. Non-integer scale factors are "
"supported but may differ from PyTorch because of existing index-selection "
"differences."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.12/site-packages/mlx/nn/layers/upsample.py:docstring
#: of mlx.nn.layers.upsample.Upsample:31
msgid ""
"For ``\"cubic\"`` mode, enabling ``antialias`` also changes the cubic kernel "
"coefficient from ``a=-0.75`` (OpenCV convention) to ``a=-0.5`` (PIL/Pillow "
"convention), matching PyTorch's behavior. This affects the interpolant "
"shape, not just the filter width."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.12/site-packages/mlx/nn/layers/upsample.py:docstring
#: of mlx.nn.layers.upsample.Upsample:36
msgid ""
"``antialias=True`` with ``align_corners=True`` is not supported and will "
"raise a ``ValueError``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../src/python/nn/_autosummary/mlx.nn.Upsample.rst:0
msgid "Parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.12/site-packages/mlx/nn/layers/upsample.py:docstring
#: of mlx.nn.layers.upsample.Upsample:39
msgid ""
"The multiplier for the spatial size. If a ``float`` is provided, it is the "
"multiplier for all spatial dimensions. Otherwise, the number of scale "
"factors provided must match the number of spatial dimensions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.12/site-packages/mlx/nn/layers/upsample.py:docstring
#: of mlx.nn.layers.upsample.Upsample:44
msgid ""
"The upsampling algorithm, either ``\"nearest\"``, ``\"linear\"`` or "
"``\"cubic\"``. Default: ``\"nearest\"``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.12/site-packages/mlx/nn/layers/upsample.py:docstring
#: of mlx.nn.layers.upsample.Upsample:47
msgid ""
"Changes the way the corners are treated during ``\"linear\"`` and "
"``\"cubic\"`` upsampling.  See the note above and the examples below for "
"more details.  Default: ``False``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../../.conda/lib/python3.12/site-packages/mlx/nn/layers/upsample.py:docstring
#: of mlx.nn.layers.upsample.Upsample:51
msgid ""
"If ``True``, apply an antialiasing filter when downsampling with "
"``\"linear\"`` or ``\"cubic\"`` mode. For ``\"cubic\"`` mode this also "
"switches the kernel coefficient to ``a=-0.5``. Not supported with "
"``\"nearest\"`` mode or with ``align_corners=True``. Default: ``False``."
msgstr ""

